CHECKS
========================================================================================================================
  [PASS] k01-1 MUTATION: turning the kernel off (nu == 1, i.e. GR + dark matter, which obeys the strong equivalence principle) must give Q_2 identically zero -- there is no anomalous quadrupole without nonlinear gravity   (q(nu=1) = 0.000e+00)
  [PASS] k01-2 MUTATION: switching OFF the external field must give Q_2 identically zero, because an isolated point mass in MOND is spherically symmetric.  This is the check that proves the signal is a strong-equivalence-principle violation and not a kernel artefact   (q(g_e = 0) = 2.757e-13)
  [PASS] k01-3 LIMIT: an external field far above a_0 must drive Q_2 to zero (the Solar System is then Newtonian out to beyond its own MOND radius)   (q(y_eN = 1e8) = 3.785e-309 vs fiducial -2.552e-01)
  [PASS] k01-4 two INDEPENDENT quadratures of the same integral -- the by-parts form (no numerical derivative anywhere) and the raw divergence form (two finite-difference derivatives) -- must agree   (by-parts -0.25520 vs divergence -0.25520, relative 1.78e-06)
  [PASS] k01-5 GRID CONVERGENCE: refining the radial and angular grids by 8x and widening the domain by two decades either side must move q by less than 0.5%   (coarse -0.25520 | fiducial -0.25520 | fine -0.25520)
  [PASS] k01-6 THE LAW'S SCALING, tested rather than asserted: q must be a function of y_e = g_e/a_0 ALONE, so that Q_2 = q a_0^{3/2}/sqrt(GM).  Recomputing at the same y_e returns the same q, and the dimensional prefactor is analytic   (q reproducible to 0.00e+00; prefactor a_0/r_M = a_0^1.5/sqrt(GM) by construction)
  [PASS] k01-7 the interior multipole expansion is legitimate: essentially none of the source lies inside 0.05 r_M = 400 AU, so the quadrupole really is harmonic where the planets are   (fraction of q from x < 0.05 (r < 398 AU): 2.58e-09)

  sensitivity of the prediction to its ONE measured input (v_c), canonical footing:
     v_c = 229 km/s -> y_e = 2.220 -> Q_2 = -1.937e-26 s^-2
     v_c = 233 km/s -> y_e = 2.298 -> Q_2 = -2.006e-26 s^-2
     v_c = 236 km/s -> y_e = 2.358 -> Q_2 = -2.058e-26 s^-2
  [PASS] k01-8 the prediction is not fragile against the one measured input: a +-3 km/s change in the local circular speed (the full spread of modern determinations) must move Q_2 by less than 25%   (spread 6.0% over v_c = 229-236 km/s)

